# A part path of the CURRENT callable, read and written inside it (Codex CODEX-U6V1-READONLY-20261018T224613Z point 4 and
# CODEX-U6V1-ROOT-PARTS-20261018T2247Z): `count\var\x` inside count is the PLACE of the explicit var field -- the published
# value, 5 at the first entry -- not x's working value; the write `count\var\x: 15` changes the place; x's working row is
# never assigned, so nothing publishes over it and the reader outside sees 15.  Natively and with the methods walked (the
# walked twin pins a four-part fn whose places hang from its code occurrence).  count() 515, then count\var\x 15; success 7;
# 81 / 82 otherwise.
fn: count () int (x: int: 5)
    int: before 0
    before: count\var\x
    count\var\x: 15
    return: before * 100 + count\var\x
end: count
fn: check () int
    if: count() != 515
        return: 81
    if: count\var\x != 15
        return: 82
    return: 7
end: check
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: check(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
